spew -- mock National Enquirer headlines========================================    spew [n] [rulesfile]spew builds nonsense headlines from a grammar of phrases and slots -- itworks, as its author put it, almost like yacc in reverse.  `spew' printsone, `spew 5' prints five.  It reads its rules from GAMES/SPEW/headline bydefault; point it at another rules file, or set RULESFILE in theenvironment, to spew other kinds of nonsense.  `spew -c file' compiles arules file to a faster compressed form.The rules-file format is described in SRC/spew/ORIG/manual.Copyright 1987 Greg Smith; permission granted to freely use anddistribute.  Originals in SRC/spew/ORIG.